    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is the ordered account of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the whole endpoint is guarded by `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; a caller without that role never enters the pipeline.\n- **Transaction** \u2014 every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all the work below commits once, at the end.\n\nThe pipeline runs 14 steps in this order:\n\n### 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 validate & normalize the body (400s)\nAccumulates a list of offending fields and throws `MissingFieldsException` (400) if any are found. In order within the step:\n1. `firstName` required (non-blank).\n2. `lastName` required (non-blank).\n3. **address** normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); if empty after normalization \u2192 error, otherwise the normalized value is written back onto the request. *(side-effect: mutates address)*\n4. `city` required (non-blank).\n5. **telephone** normalized to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; assume `+61` and drop a leading `0` if no `+`; must be 8\u201315 digits, and recognised codes checked exactly \u2014 `+61`=9 national digits, `+1`=10); `null`/invalid \u2192 error, otherwise the normalized value is written back. *(side-effect: mutates telephone)*\n6. **email** (optional) \u2014 if present: must match the email regex, must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); if valid, lower-cased and written back. *(side-effect: mutates email)*\n7. **postcode** (optional) \u2014 if present: must be exactly 4 digits **and** fall within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4-digit); if valid, trimmed value written back. *(side-effect: mutates postcode)*\n8. **registrationDate** (optional) \u2014 if present and later than today \u2192 error.\n9. On success, republishes the (mutated) request as a variable for later steps.\n\n### 2. `EnsureCityCapacity` \u2014 409 if full\nCounts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed). If \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n### 3. `EnsureDailyLimit` \u2014 429 if over limit\nCounts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today's business-day-adjusted date. If \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyLimitException` (429).\n\n### 4. `BuildOwner` \u2014 construct the entity *(side-effect)*\nMaps the validated DTO to an `Owner`. Sets `registrationDate` to the supplied date (or today if absent), **adjusted to a business day** (Sat\u2192Mon, Sun\u2192Mon).\n\n### 5. `AssignHousehold` \u2014 derive `householdId` *(side-effect)*\nIf a postcode is present, sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`. No postcode \u2192 left null.\n\n### 6. `EnsureUniqueIdentity` \u2014 the consolidated duplicate check (409)\nScans all existing owners:\n- **Full-identity duplicate** \u2014 if the `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) exactly matches an existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409). Always applies.\n- **Household duplicate** \u2014 if the computed `householdId` matches an existing owner's \u2192 409, **unless** the request set `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n### 7. `AssignHouseholdSize` \u2014 derive `householdSize` *(side-effect)*\nCounts stored owners with the same `householdId`, plus one for this new owner (1 if no household).\n\n### 8. `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 derive `customerCode` *(side-effect)*\nSets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION is derived from postcode-range (city fallback) and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n### 9. `AssignNamesakeCount` \u2014 derive `namesakeCount` *(side-effect)*\nCounts existing owners sharing the same firstName + lastName (case-insensitive); new owner not yet counted.\n\n### 10. `AssignBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 derive `bulkSignupWarning` *(side-effect)*\nSets the flag true if > 80 owners already registered today (business-day-adjusted).\n\n### 11. `AssignPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 derive soft-match flags *(side-effect)*\nIf `sharesHousehold` is true \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Otherwise, if an existing owner shares lastName + postcode but has a *different* telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = that owner's id (lowest id if several); else false/null.\n\n### 12. `SaveOwner` \u2014 persist *(side-effect)*\n`ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 assigns the generated id.\n\n### 13. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 audit log *(side-effect)*\nEmits an `AUDIT` logger info line with id, customerCode, registrationDate and derived membershipLevel.\n\n### 14. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 respond *(side-effect)*\nMaps to `OwnerDto` and sends `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Summary of the two categories, in order:**\n\n- **Validations (rejections):** required fields (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone) \u2192 400; telephone E.164 validity \u2192 400; email syntax + disposable-domain \u2192 400; postcode format + region range \u2192 400; future registrationDate \u2192 400; city capacity \u2265 50 \u2192 409; daily limit \u2265 100 \u2192 429; full-identity duplicate \u2192 409; household duplicate (unless `sharesHousehold`) \u2192 409.\n- **Side-effects (mutations/writes):** normalize address, telephone, email, postcode on the request; business-day-adjust registrationDate; derive householdId, householdSize, customerCode, namesakeCount, bulkSignupWarning, possibleDuplicate/possibleDuplicateOf; persist (save) assigning the id; emit the audit log line; send the 201 response \u2014 all committed in a single transaction.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the postcode\u2192region check in step 1 uses `Localities.region(city)` (city only), while the `customerCode` in step 8 uses `Localities.region(city, postcode)` (postcode-range first). You didn't ask about correctness, so I'm only noting the two derivations use different region logic."
